1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Gjesling i Store Norske Leksikon https://snl.no/Gjesling
2 CONT
2 CONT Gjesling (or Gjæsling) was an old family at Vågå in Oppland, Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1130 Ivar Gjesling was the earliest-known owner of the farm Sandbu (just north of Vågåmo) in Vågå. He served as King Magnus IV's lendmann (governor) for the Opplands. Ivar Gjesling, allied himself with the Birchlegs (Birkebeine
2 CONC rne) — who chose Sverre as their king at Øreting in 1177. Sverre granted him the valley of Heidal as a reward.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigrid Undset's fictional Lady Ragnfrid, wife of Lavrans, was create a Gjesling from Sandbu.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gjesling descendants still own land in the Vågå region, Riddersandbu, which includes buildings built before 1600.
