1 OCCU Dommer i Bjerkreim og lagrettemann
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Alias Orm fra Stokka. Han levde en periode på Stokka i Vats. Han bodde der i 1591, men var tilbake på Byre i 1599. Orm var en av de rikeste i Ryfylke på siste del av 1500-tallet. Han eide en anselig mengde jordegod
2 CONC s, inkludert Stokka på Vats.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Odelsgodset i Marvik høyrde til Orm i Byre sitt gods. Orm levde på 1500 talet. Ættlingar etter han brukar framleies br.nr. 1 av Marvik. Fleire av brukarane i Marvik var lensmenn i Jelsa, og Marvik var då ofte nytta til tingstad f
2 CONC or skipreidet."
2 CONT
2 CONT Orm var utsending til kongehyldningen i 1591.
2 CONT
2 CONT Barn:
2 CONT
2 CONT NN Ormsdatter Byre 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marite Ormsdatter Byre Jørstad 
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna OrmsdatterByre 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ånund (Anund) Ormson Byre Marvik 
2 CONT
2 CONT Olav Ormson Byre Vatland
2 CONT
2 CONT  Orm Åmundsson was one of the best known and wealthiest men in Ryfylke in the last half of the 1500's. He appears to have been from the island of Byre in Finnøy parish and was probably living there in 1563. Byre belonged to a nobl
2 CONC e family, so Orm was leasing it from them. However, he owned a considerable amount of land around Ryfylke, including Stokka in Vats. Orm was named at Stokka in 1591, but was back at Byre in 1599. He was one of the 12 lagrettemenn 
2 CONC who chose the area's representives to the coronation of King Christian IV.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 2 3 
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: ABT 1515 in Byre gård #16, Fister, Rogaland, Norway 
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 1601 in Byre gård #16, Fister, Rogaland, Norway
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Orm Åmundsson was one of the best known and wealthiest men in Ryfylke in the last half of the 1500's. He appears to have been from the
2 CONT
2 CONT island of Byre in Finnøy parish and was probably living there in 1563. Byre belonged to a noble family, so Orm was leasing it from them.
2 CONT
2 CONT However, he owned a considerable amount of land around Ryfylke, including Stokka in Vats. Orm was named at Stokka in 1591, but was
2 CONT
2 CONT back at Byre in 1599. He was one of the 12 lagrettemenn who chose the area's representives to the coronation of King Christian IV.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 2 3 
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: ABT 1515 in Byre gård #16, Fister, Rogaland, Norway 
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 1601 in Byre gård #16, Fister, Rogaland, Norway
