2 CONT Title: Byre 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Orm Åmundsson was one of the best known and wealthiest men in Ryfylke in the last half of the 1500's. He appears to have been from the
2 CONT
2 CONT island of Byre in Finnøy parish and was probably living there in 1563. Byre belonged to a noble family, so Orm was leasing it from them.
2 CONT
2 CONT However, he owned a considerable amount of land around Ryfylke, including Stokka in Vats. Orm was named at Stokka in 1591, but was
2 CONT
2 CONT back at Byre in 1599. He was one of the 12 lagrettemenn who chose the area's representives to the coronation of King Christian IV.
2 CONT
