1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://www.digitalarkivet.no/ft10041005141063 Manntallet 1666]: Øfreby, Opsidder Niels Andersen, 46 år
2 CONT
2 CONT Har antakelig, sammen med broren Halvor, overtatt Øvrebø av kongen (Kristian IV) i bytte med den delen av Eig som Kristiansand skulle bygges på
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT translated from the Norwegian by Google: (Norwegian cousins feel free to improve on this!) I suspect "hides" is a measure of land
2 CONT =============================
2 CONT
2 CONT The father Anders Olson Oak has enough makeover shifted so he gave up some hides in oak (Eg at Kristiansand) to the king and regained including Øvrebø. Nils and his brother Halvor Derev first his father's farm at Eg along with cou
2 CONC sin Gunnar Paulsen who was the son of an brother Anders Eik.
2 CONT
2 CONT Besides Oak Anders had sons 3 hides in Midthus, Grim and 1 1/2 skin Landås in Iveland. They had 2 hides in Hoyland Lista. As consideration for bygrunnen got the 4 hides in Øvrebø in Øvrebø, 1 skin Sangesland in Øvrebø and 3 hides 
2 CONC in Klepland Søgne.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1645 the sons of Anders; Nils Halvor owners of three hides in Øvrebø and Sangesland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother Halvor drifted first farm in Øvrebø. In 1659 we find Nils which uses the farm in Øvrebø.
2 CONT
2 CONT He bought Greipesland. Later he left Greipesland son Anders Nilsson Øvrebø. The farm was solved from the crown in 1663 of Appeal Laurids Andersen Undal. He sold one consumption, 1 1/2 hides, the same year Nils who stayed at Øvrebø
2 CONC . The other consumption, also 1 1/2 hides, was bought by Omund Ulvson Ugland. Both sales are registered 04/23/1664. Omund Ulvson (mentioned Hegseide by Heisel Vennesla) sold its use in 1683 to the sons of Nils Bernt Anders Nilsson
2 CONC ner.
2 CONT
2 CONT Greipesland was released from the crown in 1663 of Appeal Laurids Andersen Undal. He sold one consumption, "Der aust" br.nr. 1 on Greipesland Nils Anderson Øverebø who stayed at Øverebø.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1674 owned Nils 11/2 skin Greipesland and 3 goatskin Rolle Stad. Nils handed Greipesland to the eldest son Anders Nilsson Øvrebø who was married Ingjerd Gunstein Daughter Stray.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1682 owned Nils 2 hides in Engeland, 1.5 hides in Greipesland, 1 skin Sangesland, 3 goatskin Rolle Stad and 1/2 goatskin in Opsal. Son Ansten got farm Engeland. Son Change inherited Sangesland (3. consumption). It went into "De
2 CONC r heime" in 1795.
