1 NAME Ole Rasmussen /Røssum/
2 GIVN Ole Rasmussen
2 _MARNM Røssum
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1570
2 PLAC Røssum gård, Kvam
2 ADDR
3 STAE Oppland
3 CTRY Norway
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1652
2 PLAC Røssum gård
2 ADDR
3 CITY Kvam, Gudbrandsdal
3 STAE Østlandet
3 CTRY Norge
1 OCCU Røssum gård
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} His name is sometimes spelled Ole and sometimes Oluf. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ole Rasmusssen leased in 1610 half a hide of church property in Røssum, but supposedly owned 8 hides in the Farm already.  His property division took place on April 1, 1652 so we have to assume that he was dead at that time.
2 CONT
2 CONT As far as we know, he had 5 sons, presumably he also had duaghters, but about these we don't know anything for certain.  State archieve clerk Thomle writes that Ole Rasmussen  Røssum could not have come from the Gjesling family, t
2 CONC o which the name Rasmus is well known,. On the other hand, writes Thomle, is it possible that his wife or his mother, possibly could have been the woman Eldri who in 1644 owned 8 hides in Røssum, and could have been conected with 
2 CONC family ties to the inhabitants of the farm in the 1500's. because among his sons we find both an Iver and a Amund, that could point to the family ties, but about this we know nothing for certain. He did however own part of the Ros
2 CONC sum Farm.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.genealogi.no/NST/pdf/nst_1_1927_thomle_ocr.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT http://homepages.rootsweb.com/~norway/na27.html Information about how the farms were bought by farmers from the King.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://homepages.rootsweb.com/~norway/na17.html Norweigen/English dictionary
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.valdressamband.org/archive/avisen.html Farm Info
