1 NAME Ola Olsen /Slette/
2 GIVN Ola Olsen
2 _MARNM Slette
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 12 APR 1680
2 PLAC Slette 
2 ADDR
3 STAE Oppland
3 POST Vågå
3 CTRY Norge
1 DEAT
2 DATE MAR 1758
2 PLAC Slette 
2 ADDR
3 STAE Oppland
3 CTRY Norge
1 OCCU Large farmer and owned the Slette Farm/Storbonde og einde Slette gård
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Fam. Slette and Ovren, next to Fliflet are nearest related to Björnstjerne Björnson.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is said that Ovren shall have been Gausdal’s mightiest family, all from Östen Ovren’s calculations, and those of Föxen farm had the greatest prosperity.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ole Olsen Slette was born 12/4 - 1680 at Slette farm in Heidal, and inherited as sole son his father’s immense farmland, Slette, on 5 huder with lease and assets, in addition to 8 Skind in Horgan. In 1723 he also owned the farms L
2 CONC ien and Bilben. On 16/7 - 1728 he bought from Nils Bygfulien, Aurdal in Valdres, Öistad farm in Storbygden at Land, 5 huder with lease over 1 hud (which belonged to the church) and underlying place, Tronholt, 2 Skind all together 
2 CONC for 1600 Riksdaler. In 1744 he divided inheritance between himself and his wife on the one side, and his 5 sons on the other. As a consequence of that division he owned: 1. His father’s farm, Slette, in Heidal. 5 huder, appraised 
2 CONC at 650 Riksdaler.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Öistad farm in Land, 5 huder, appraised at 550 Riksdaler.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. In Sandbu farm in Bredebygden 1½ hud, appraised at 350 Riksdaler.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. In Nedre Bilben farm in Heidal 1½ hud, appraised at 150 Riksdaler. "In consideration that the farmhouse is dilapidated and used in common under Slette."
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Lien farm in Heidal, 1 hud, appraised at 50 Riksdaler. In all, 15 huder, appraised at 1750 Riksdaler. For these field lands he settled with his sons for 350 Riksdaler each. But in addition, he possessed:
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Söndre Hagen farm in Heidal, which had 3 horses and 20 cows.
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Koloen farm in Bredebygden in Vågå, which had 1 horse and 10 cows. These possessions he kept for himself and his wife and those on whose shoulders it would fall: They, of the children, who attended to them the best upon their o
2 CONC ld age. According to the register of 1723, he owned in all 34 horses, 186 cows and 362 småfe [small beasts]. About 1706 he was married to Anne Pedersdatter Horgen, who was born at Horgen in Heidal circa 1681, and died in April, 17
2 CONC 50. She had 5 sons, namely:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Ole Olsen Slette (circa 1707 - 1775). Married Kari Paulsdatter Tolstad (circa 1703 - 1775). He inherited his father’s farm, Slette, and in 1845 bought Bilben and in 1749, Lien from his brother. Later, he obtained from his paren
2 CONC ts, Horgen and Koloen farms. In 1727 he bought from the King, 1 Skind in the cleared lands, Rusten in Övre Heidal in Vågå. In 1733 he sold this again. In 1727 he bought from the King for 1590 Riksdaler courant12, 2 Huder with leas
2 CONC e including remaining farm debt, 1 hud and 3 Skind in Lillejivne farm (little Hiem) with underlying Landverk in Kvam. Then, he sold the farm again in 1737 to Tosten Olsen Hielle at Dovre for 1200 Riksdaler.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Peder Olsen Öistad. (circa 1713 - 1793). He inherited Öistad farm in Land. In 1736 he was married to Anna Dorothea Kristensdatter Fliflet (1717 - 1763), daughter of Lieutenant Kristen Fliflet and Eli Stenersdatter Waalen.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Torsten Olsen Slette. (circa 1719 - ? ). Inherited Sandbu in Bredebygden, later with his father’s death, also Söndre Horgen. The latter he sold to his nephew [brother’s son], Iver Olsen Slette for 60 Riksdaler. He was no doubt 
2 CONC unmarried.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Östen Olsen Ovren. (1721 - 1801)
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Iver Olsen Vigness. (1724 - 1780). Inherited Lien in Heidal, and part of Slette, but later saved the latter for his brother, Ole. In 1748 he bought Lillejevne in Kvam, but then sold it the same year. In 1749, he bought Ovren fa
2 CONC rm in Gausdal from Captain Cold for 1450 Riksdaler and lived there until he sold this to his brother, Östen, in 1758 for 2300 Riksdaler. Since then, he lived at Vigness in Fåberg. He was married the first time in 1745 to Kristine 
2 CONC Jörgensdatter Elstad (1724 - 1755), daughter of Jörgen Olsen Elstad and Anne Stenersdatter Waalen. Another time, he was married (1756) to Marie Pedersdatter Wignæs (1734 ? ) who earlier had been married to Christian Henningsen Wig
2 CONC næs (1724 - 1756).
2 CONT
2 CONT OVREN - RÖSEM AND SLETTE Bygdelag
2 CONT
